.TH FILIN 1 "October 2026" "opendrop-rs" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
filin \- Apple Wireless Direct Link (AWDL) link layer for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filin
.BI -i " interface"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B filin
creates a TAP interface (normally
.BR awdl0 )
and bridges Ethernet traffic to Apple Wireless Direct Link frames transmitted
through a monitor-mode Wi-Fi interface.
.PP
Normal operation requires CAP_NET_ADMIN and CAP_NET_RAW, or equivalent root
privileges. The Wi-Fi adapter and driver must support monitor mode and raw frame
injection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -i " interface"
Wi-Fi monitor interface. This option is required.
.TP
.BI -c " channel"
AWDL anchor/social channel. The default is 44.
.TP
.BI -h " interface"
Name of the TAP interface to create. The default is awdl0.
.TP
.BR -N ", " --assume-monitor
Do not change the radio to monitor mode; assume it is already configured.
.TP
.B --check
Probe the selected adapter for monitor-mode capability and exit.
.TP
.B --no-http
Disable the local introspection HTTP server.
.TP
.BI --http-addr " address"
Set the loopback introspection address. The default is 127.0.0.1:9930.
.TP
.B --park
Stay on the selected anchor channel instead of channel hopping.
.TP
.BR -f ", " --no-rssi-filter
Disable RSSI admission filtering.
.TP
.BR -M ", " --force-master
Force filin to win the AWDL master election. This is enabled by default.
.TP
.B --no-force-master
Use the normal AWDL election instead.
.TP
.BI --tx-retransmits " count"
Re-inject each unicast data frame the requested number of extra times.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
sudo filin -i wlan1 -c 44 -h awdl0
luftlift -i awdl0 receive -o ./incoming
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR luftlift (1),
.BR ip (8),
.BR tcpdump (8)
